TEXT -96 -352 Left 2 ;Problem 2.3 - the driver of 2.2 as a source, pushed by a 10 N Lorentz force.  Left: impedance analogy.  Right: mobility analogy.
TEXT -96 -320 Left 2 ;Top row: force source (Thevenin / Norton), bottom row: the equivalent velocity source.  The load is a damper R_L; RL = 1u is a free cone.
TEXT -96 -272 Left 2 !.param Mm=20m Cm=1m Rm=0.5 F=10 RL=1u
TEXT -96 176 Left 2 ;(A) Thevenin: f_Th = 10 N in series with Z_M.  u = I(Vu_A)
TEXT -96 896 Left 2 ;(B) Norton: u_No = f_Th/Z_M (G source, Laplace) in parallel with Z_M.  u = I(Vu_B);  u_No(f0) = 10/0.5 = 20 m/s
TEXT 1344 176 Left 2 ;(C) Norton: f_No = 10 N in parallel with Y_M.  u = V(uC)
TEXT 1344 896 Left 2 ;(D) Thevenin: u_Th = Y_M f_No (E source, Laplace) in series with Y_M.  u = V(uD)
TEXT -96 1008 Left 2 !.ac dec 1000 1 1k
TEXT -96 1056 Left 2 ;Plot I(Vu_A), I(Vu_B), V(uC), V(uD) on a LINEAR axis: four identical curves, 20 m/s at f0 = 35.6 Hz.  Change RL: they stay identical.
